  ("C", [Sixty. A is the number in each of the other three subjects, B is an invention, and D is the total for a four-subject sitting.]),
  ("B", [The reading text: ten questions from a closed book, answerable in four minutes. A is the long, expensive first passage; C needs the passage read; D is a good second choice, not a first.]),
  ("C", [Flag and return. A gives away a quarter of a mark; B abandons the elimination you could still do; D is how candidates lose eight minutes to one question.]),
  ("B", [Blanks first — they are the only certain loss. Spelling and handwriting are not marked by the engine, and the numbering is automatic.]),
